<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Zou</h1><p class="st-meta">1046 BCE – 261 BCE (approx.) · capital Zou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Shandong state, called Zhu and later Zou, that endured for eight centuries beside Lu and was the homeland of the philosopher Mencius.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Zhu was ruled by the Cao clan, said to descend from the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhuanxu">Zhuanxu</a>, and was recognised by the Zhou as a minor state in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, just south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qufu">Qufu</a>. Its rulers initially held only the low rank of viscount.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Zhu fought frequent border wars with its larger neighbour, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-lu">State of Lu</a>, while balancing between Qi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> and later Chu. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-wen-of-zhu">Duke Wen of Zhu</a> moved the capital to Yi in 614 BCE after divination, saying the ruler's task was to benefit the people. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> the state was known as Zou, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mencius">Mencius</a> was born there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Zou survived into the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> before being annexed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/state-of-chu">State of Chu</a> around 261 BCE. Its name lives on in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoucheng">Zoucheng</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-mencius">Mencius Temple</a> and the tombs of the Meng family still stand.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-zou.jpg" alt="State of Zou" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Streitende-Reiche2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-fa